            <ArticleTitle>Complete Genome Sequence of a Papaya ringspot virus Isolate from South Korea That Infects Cucurbita pepo.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e01289-17</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/genomeA.01289-17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The complete genome sequence of a Papaya ringspot virus (PRSV) isolate from South Korea (SK) infecting squash (Cucurbita pepo) was obtained using paired-end RNA sequencing. A BLASTn search of the PRSV SK isolate full-genome sequence showed nucleotide sequence identity ranging from 81% to 83% with previously reported PRSV isolates (GenBank accession numbers KX655874 and EF017707).</AbstractText>
